course: dictionary
lesson: 3686
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives each meaning its own number, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «A flamingo feeds with its head upside down in the water.» Here a flamingo is the bird.
explain: Flamingo has a second meaning too: a plastic flamingo is a pink garden ornament. Read the clues. If the sentence talks about water, lakes or feeding, it means the bird. If it talks about a lawn or a garden, it may mean the ornament.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put the bird meaning in «The flamingo fed on tiny shrimps» and it makes sense. Put the ornament meaning in and it does not. Try both meanings and see which one fits.
fact: A flamingo is a tall wading bird with long thin legs, a long bendy neck, pink feathers and a curved beak.
fact: Flamingos live in big groups by lakes and lagoons.
fact: Flamingos often stand on one leg, and they feed with their heads upside down.
fact: Flamingos get their pink from the pink-coloured food they eat, like tiny shrimps and algae.
fact: A plastic flamingo is a pink garden ornament, and it is a joke symbol of fancy American gardens.
exercise: «A flamingo feeds with its head upside down in the water.» Which meaning of flamingo is this? | A type of shrimp | A pink garden ornament | *A tall wading bird | A lawn chair
exercise: «Zoos add pink colouring to flamingos' food, or the birds slowly fade.» Why do zoos add pink colouring? | So the birds grow taller | *So the birds stay pink | So the birds can stand on one leg | So the birds can fly faster
exercise: Which meaning of flamingo fits «The pink flamingo stood on the lawn beside the shed»? | A bird that wades in lakes | A type of shrimp | *A plastic garden ornament | A bird with a bendy neck
test: A group of flamingos is sometimes called what? | A gaggle | A murder | *A flamboyance | A herd
test: Why are flamingos pink? | Because they live in the sun | *Because of the pink-coloured food they eat | Because the water is pink | Because they paint themselves
exam: In «A real flamingo's long neck is soft and bends», what does the word real tell you? | It means the plastic garden ornament | It means a pink zoo painting | It means a flamingo shaped like a shrimp | *It means the living bird, not the ornament
